.TH GIT-PROFILE 1
.SH NAME
git-profile \- select a Git identity for the current repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git profile
.RI [ profile | command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Selects a named Git profile for the current repository, or returns it to
automatic profile selection. With no argument, displays the explicit profile,
previous profile, and effective identity.
.PP
Profiles are ordinary Git configuration files stored in:
.PP
.nf
~/.config/git/profiles/
.fi
.PP
The filename is the profile name. For example:
.PP
.nf
~/.config/git/profiles/personal
~/.config/git/profiles/work
~/.config/git/profiles/fedora
.fi
.SH LOCAL CONFIGURATION
Selecting
.B git profile fedora
adds the profile include and remembers the prior selection in that repository's
.BR .git/config :
.PP
.nf
[include]
    path = ~/.config/git/profiles/fedora
[profile]
    previous = default
.fi
.PP
.B default
is a built-in pseudo-profile meaning that no local profile include is present.
It exposes the identity selected by the global defaults and remote-owner rules.
.PP
Only
.B include.path
values inside the profiles directory are managed. Unrelated local includes and
settings are left untouched. The single
.B profile.previous
value exists only to implement previous-profile switching; no global history or
state file is maintained.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.I profile
Select the named profile. Any file in the profiles directory can be selected.
.TP
.B list
List available profiles.
.TP
.B \-
Switch to the previous profile in this repository. The profile being left
becomes the new previous profile, so repeated invocations toggle between the
two most recent selections.
.TP
.BR default , " reset" , " unset"
Switch to the built-in default profile by removing the repository-local profile
include. The profile being reset remains available through
.BR "git profile \-" .
.TP
.B show
Display the explicit and previous profiles. The explicit profile is
.B default
when profile selection is automatic.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-config (1),
.BR git-whoami (1)
